From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dariusz Majnert <dariusz@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 1 Jul 2026 00:57:53 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] emc: add resumable Stop for active AUTO programs

Add a dedicated task and trajectory Stop operation that preserves interpreter and motion queues. Stop safely completes position-synchronized motion, snapshots spindle and coolant outputs, and restores them before resuming queued motion, while still waiting for interrupted orientation to complete. Expose the command and Stop state through Python and HALUI; Node bindings are maintained in the consumer repository.

Ported to v2.10.0-pre2. Differences from the patch on the old base:

- Upstream M5 arms motion's next-feed at-speed barrier and EMCMOT_SPINDLE_OFF now overwrites atspeed_next_feed. Stop turns spindles off with EMCMOT_SPINDLE_AT_SPEED_PRESERVE, which SPINDLE_OFF now honours as SPINDLE_ON already did, so a barrier armed before Stop still holds the next feed after Resume.
- Stop is accepted while task waits for a queued G28.2 homing cycle (motion is dipped into FREE, so task.mode reads MANUAL). The homing cycle runs to completion before Stop reaches STOPPED.
- The trajectory planner judged rest from emcmotStatus->current_vel after tpUpdateInitialStatus() had zeroed it, so STOPPED was reported, and spindle and coolant switched off, while a feed was still decelerating. It now uses the segment velocities.
- motion-logger logs EMCMOT_STOP.
- Stop turns spindles off and on with a PRESERVE request that no longer stays behind in the shared motion command, so a later S-word change still arms the next feed's at-speed wait.
- While stopping, the planner does not start a held segment from rest. Starting it consumed a pending at-speed wait, or began a G33 index search, while Stop had the spindle off; the feed then resumed without waiting, or the thread locked on during coast-down and the axis raced to catch up after Resume.
- Stop lets the whole run of position-synchronized segments that share one spindle synchronization finish, not only the segment active when it arrived. Halting at the start of the next G33 left the axis behind the turning spindle and Resume lunged to catch up.
- Resume or Run during a Stop always leaves single-step mode entered by an earlier Step.
- EMCMOT_ABORT ends a Stop in every motion mode, and the planner drops its pointer to the synchronized segment when that run is over or the queue empties.
- motion-logger logs EMCMOT_STOP.
- tests/resumable-stop gains the scenarios dwell-atspeed, homing, homing-interrupted, speed-change-atspeed, queued-feed-atspeed, g33-chain and step-resume-stopping, fails if STOPPED is reported while moving, re-runs three scenarios under the trapezoidal planner, and its checkresult now fails when the scenario count is wrong.
