diff --git a/tests/resumable-stop/README b/tests/resumable-stop/README
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..ee83269
--- /dev/null
+++ b/tests/resumable-stop/README
@@ -0,0 +1,30 @@
+Verify resumable Stop preserves an active AUTO program and resumes or
+single-steps it.
+
+This regression test exercises the task-level Stop operation directly through
+the Python command API. It checks that an active feed move stops without
+aborting queued AUTO state, that spindle and coolant outputs are disabled
+while stopped, and that Resume restores them before continuing the same
+program to completion. test.ini selects the jerk-limited trajectory planner
+(PLANNER_TYPE = 1) for every scenario, although position-synchronized moves
+(G33, G76, G33.1) always use the trapezoidal planner; the ordinary,
+single-step and fperrev scenarios run a second time with the default
+trapezoidal planner (PLANNER_TYPE = 0). Every run rejects zero-limit Ruckig
+fallback errors, which the G95 scenario could provoke while spindle feedback
+recovers after Resume. The dwell-atspeed scenario checks that a
+spindle at-speed barrier armed before Stop still holds the next feed after
+Resume. The homing scenario issues Stop during a queued G28.2
+and checks that the homing cycle completes before the program holds in
+STOPPED.
+The homing-interrupted scenario ends a queued G28.2 early by Abort, E-stop,
+machine off, a mode change, and Stop followed at once by Abort and AUTO, and
+checks that a later program runs, that Stop is rejected for an MDI command
+and that it still reaches STOPPED in a new AUTO program.
+The speed-change-atspeed scenario checks that an S-word after two Stop and
+Resume cycles still makes the next feed wait for spindle at-speed.
+The queued-feed-atspeed scenario stops while a queued feed waits for spindle
+at-speed and checks that the feed still waits for at-speed after Resume.
+The g33-chain scenario stops during the first of two consecutive G33 moves
+and checks that Stop lets both finish before STOPPED.
+The step-resume-stopping scenario sends Step and then Resume while Stop waits
+for G33 and checks that the program then runs on without single-stepping.
